      "id": 1,
      "text": "Rosholt was incorporated in 1907 and named after John Gilbert Rosholt, who built the town's first sawmill in 1884.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosholt%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Gottlieb Stanbly first owned the land where Rosholt sits after receiving four parcels from the government in 1858.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosholt%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Jens Rasmussen created a millpond by damming Flume Creek to build a water-driven feed mill in the late 1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosholt%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The arrival of the railroad helped Rosholt grow, with Brooks and Ross Lumber playing a key role in bringing it here.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
